  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New `assets/machines/g-edm.mch`, the \"G-EDM Wire EDM (template)\":\n  - It is kind `wire_edm`, with a table with X and Y and a `guides` head.\n  - It has `edm.awt: false` and `controller.post: \"G-EDM Wire EDM\"`. The Setup page offers that post (#2374). The mount does not change the post.\n  - It states no travel, no rapid, no guide height, no taper, no wire diameters, no `edm.codes` and no conditions. Each G-EDM build is different, and the unstated-limits law (`assets/machines/AGENTS.md`) forbids a guess.\n  - The description names gedm.org. It tells the user to enter the travels, the guide heights and the measured spark gaps in the Machine editor.\n- The template is registered in `MACHINES` and `embedded()` (`crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`).\n- `site/content/guide/check-and-post/machines.md` and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` name the template.\n- The decision file is `docs/decisions/2701-g-edm-template.md`.\n\nThe tests are in the existing G-EDM suite (`crates/app/tests/g_edm_post.rs`), not in a new top-level file. `punch_doc` now has a `punch_on(machine_text, ...)` form.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `g_edm_post::the_g_edm_template_validates_and_states_no_invented_limit`: library entry, kind, units, `validate_text` clean, axes without travel or rapid, no guide height or taper, no conditions, no `edm.codes`, `awt` false, the named post, `post_serves`, and the description.\n- `g_edm_post::the_g_edm_template_refuses_a_cut_until_a_condition_is_stated`: as shipped, a Wire Contour on condition R1 is refused by the condition's name (#531). With one synthetic condition, the cut is created and posts through the app gate.\n- `machine_library` (17 tests) passes with the new entry, which includes `every_shipped_machine_lists_and_validates_clean` and `every_machine_file_in_assets_is_in_the_library`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, head 78957ac9c): 21 steps, 1 failed. The failure was `example_catalog` (`catalog_3d_rough_finish::rebuilds` and `::regenerates`), which ran over its 60 s time budget. A heavy release run on the same machine loaded the CPU at that time. Alone, the two tests pass in 34 s. They do not read the machine library.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-app -- -D warnings`: the first run found `err_expect` in the new test. 05f12e41a fixes it. Clippy is clean on the final head, and `g_edm_post` (11 tests) passes.\n- Site tests (`python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`): no failure that main does not have.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real G-EDM controller. The post output was not verified on one (as for #2700).\n- The heavy lanes: no generator or post script changes.\n\nChangelog: Machines: a \"G-EDM Wire EDM (template)\" machine for DIY G-EDM wire builds. It names the G-EDM post and states no travel, guide height or condition. Enter your build's data and measured spark gaps in the Machine editor before you cut.\n\nFixes #2701\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
